<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottokar IV of Styria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1163–1192</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ottokar IV was the last of the Otakar rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> and its first duke, raised to that rank by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> in 1180. Childless and ill, he concluded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgenberg-pact">Georgenberg Pact</a> in 1186, leaving Styria to the Babenberg dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, who inherited on his death in 1192.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottokar-iv-of-styria.jpg" alt="Ottokar IV of Styria" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Ottokar_IV_of_Styria_(127907085).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
